<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices flat or just down.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices flat or just down.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of Polish T-bills held flat or inched down by one grosz at Monday's primary auction on total demand of 1.578 billion zlotys against a 1.6 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold 1.19 billion zlotys worth of bills.  </p>
<p> T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p> new min price   96.85    94.98    90.23     ---     82.17</p>
<p> (pvs auction)  (96.85)  (94.98)  (90.24)    ---    (82.18)</p>
<p> new max price   96.90    95.10    90.30     ---     82.23</p>
<p> (pvs auction)  (97.14)  (95.35)  (90.48)    ---    (82.37)</p>
<p> offer	     300.0    300.0    200.0     ---     800.0</p>
<p> bids recorded   265.2    272.9    246.4     ---     793.4</p>
<p> bids accepted   149.6    219.1    199.9     ---     621.2</p>
<p> next auction     ---     200.0     ---     900.0     ---</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
